   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100070,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700490,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "THE PRIMARY CLIENT API",
   "originalText": "THE PRIMARY CLIENT API",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "cn2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1080,
   "width": 1011,
   "height": 65,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100071,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700497,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "SMTP is non-negotiable - it is the federation layer. But for YOUR OWN clients, HTTP wins on extensibility: IMAP's command set\nis fixed and ancient, with no vocabulary for labels-instead-of-folders, snooze, conversation threading, server-side smart\ncategorization, or push to a browser. Every one of those would need a protocol extension no client supports. A REST/JSON API\nover HTTPS lets the product evolve, works in a browser, and pairs naturally with WebSocket for push.",
   "originalText": "SMTP is non-negotiable - it is the federation layer. But for YOUR OWN clients, HTTP wins on extensibility: IMAP's command set\nis fixed and ancient, with no vocabulary for labels-instead-of-folders, snooze, conversation threading, server-side smart\ncategorization, or push to a browser. Every one of those would need a protocol extension no client supports. A REST/JSON API\nover HTTPS lets the product evolve, works in a browser, and pairs naturally with WebSocket for push.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "cn3",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1172,
   "width": 1019,
   "height": 48,
   "strokeColor": "#b45309",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100072,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700504,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "The cost is real and worth stating: you must STILL implement IMAP and POP3 for users with existing mail clients, so you end up\nmaintaining three client protocols instead of one. A deliberate trade - pay for legacy support, do not let it constrain the\nproduct.",
   "originalText": "The cost is real and worth stating: you must STILL implement IMAP and POP3 for users with existing mail clients, so you end up\nmaintaining three client protocols instead of one. A deliberate trade - pay for legacy support, do not let it constrain the\nproduct.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "d4",
